                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 72.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Hall</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-13"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 13,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Hall is instructed to inform the minister for foreign, affairs of Guatemala
                    that the telegram of acting President Barrillas is acknowledged by the
                    President, who urgently recommends that the present difficulties be brought to a
                    peaceful termination.</p>
            </div>
